  "answer": "Canberra is in the Australian Capital Territory (ACT). The ACT's unemployment rate was **4.7%** in September 2026 (original, not seasonally adjusted).\n\nThe monthly figure moves around a lot. Over the 12 months from October 2025 to September 2026 it averaged about 4.1%, ranging from 3.3% (December 2025) to 4.8% (April 2026). The rate rose 0.3 percentage points over the period shown from July 2025 (4.3%).\n\nI couldn't get a seasonally adjusted series for the ACT, so these figures are unadjusted.",
